  "notes": [
    {"topic": "multiband group delay", "text": "Multiband group delay (comp.bands = 3). Latency stays 0: the split is minimum-phase and nothing is buffered, so no latency is reported. It still delays low frequencies. At the default crossovers (88.3 Hz and 2500 Hz) and 48 kHz the group delay peaks at about 304 samples (6.3 ms) near 57 Hz, is 253 samples at 88.3 Hz and 9 samples at 2500 Hz, and stays above 1 sample from DC up to about 8150 Hz. In time it grows about as 1/xLo as the low crossover moves down (the sum of two all-pass sections of the split). Method: impulse response of the whole path with every band neutral, group delay = minus the phase slope over a +-0.1% frequency step, swept on a log grid from 10 Hz to 16 kHz. Stated to +-2 samples at the peak and +-3% at the 1-sample edge. Stated here, outside OperatorProperties, until FOUNDATIONS offers a field (SPEC A14 item 5)."}
  ],
